{
    "comments": [
        {
            "author": "Miles Jaworski",
            "date": "Mon Jul 3, 2023 at 1:25 pm",
            "comment": "I had a lot of fun with this game, it was interesting trying to find out how to get the hearts to randomize and all that."
        },
        {
            "author": "Isaac Ramos",
            "date": "Wed Jul 5, 2023 at 3:10 pm",
            "comment": "you can use the random function on google sheets. typing in =RAND() will get you a random decimal between 1 and 0. =ROUND(RAND()) will get you a 1 or a 0 randomly, and you can use this to get nearly any range. For example =ROUND(RAND()*6) will get you a random (rounded) number between 0 and 6, and =ROUND(RAND()*10)+10 will get you a number between 10 and 20."
        },
        {
            "author": "Isaac Ramos",
            "date": "Wed Jul 5, 2023 at 2:58 pm",
            "comment": "I had a lot of fun with customizing the game, I replaced the spiko and heart with my own art. I found it interesting that you could drag an object from one branch and drop it in the frame. Using this, I made it so you could move spiko on the winning frame (the platform was motionless) to add a little more flare."
        },
        {
            "author": "Miles Jaworski",
            "date": "Thu Jul 6, 2023 at 12:10 pm",
            "comment": "I did some similar stuff with mine as well, you could get a thousand points when you hit a tiny blue heart that only appears every 10 seconds and moves around. This project in general has probably been my favorite to mess around with."
        },
        {
            "author": "Tanish Kanga",
            "date": "Today at 9:58 am",
            "comment": "That sound like something fun to do when creating the video game so you could have a different image of something as the heart and depending on the style of the game it could look funny or really cool with the design."
        },
        {
            "author": "Tanish Kanga",
            "date": "Today at 9:56 am",
            "comment": "What I found interesting was how Physics could be used in making a video game. I didn't know you could use velocity and acceleration to help with the movement of objects."
        }
    ]
}

